  assign comp_search_blobs = 'young archie art flagship the little sibling of the archibald, australia’s most prestigious portrait prize. kids paint, draw or pastel a portrait of someone who matters to them - a parent, a grandparent, a best friend - and finalists hang in the art gallery of nsw alongside the grown-ups. art national|wild at art art flagship run by the australian conservation foundation. kids pick an aussie threatened species, create art that tells its story, and help raise awareness for some of our most at-risk wildlife. judges look for emotional connection over technical skill - exactly what kid art does best. art,environment national|operation art art flagship a nsw classic with a beautiful purpose. kids create artwork, and 50 pieces are gifted each year to the children’s hospital at westmead - actually hung in the wards to lift sick kids’ spirits. every entry is framed and exhibited in a nsw gallery. more than 10,000 visitors see the exhibitions each year. art nsw|cossack children’s art awards art flagship a regional wa gem. each child gets a free 30x30cm canvas to paint, and finalists are exhibited at the galbraith store in cossack alongside the famous cossack art awards. category winners receive $100, the overall winner takes home $300 plus a 50% framing discount. plus art packs from paintbox for highly commendeds. art wa - regional only|shaun tan award for young artists art flagship named after picture book legend shaun tan (the arrival, the lost thing). winners’ work hangs in a month-long public exhibition at subiaco library, professionally framed or mounted. the city of subiaco picks up the framing tab. no ai-generated work allowed. art wa|nunga kids art competition art flagship run by the commissioner for aboriginal children and young people in sa. a safe, celebrated space for first nations kids to express themselves through creative artwork on the year’s national aboriginal and torres strait islander children’s day theme. all artwork displayed at the commissioner’s office during naidoc week. art,culture sa|faber-castell create your mark art brand-led a whole-class crowd-pleaser. faber-castell partners with cool australia to build a curriculum-aligned brief for aussie classrooms - kids create using faber-castell products around themes like ’create your mark for a brighter future.’ the school of the most inspiring entries scores $1,500 worth of faber-castell products. art national|spencil art prize art brand-led run by aussie kids’ stationery brand spencil. major prize packs worth $400 each plus 20 runner-up prizes and weekly staff picks. the prize pack includes get arty colouring sets, silky crayons, art smock, sketchbook and more - so the prize itself is fuel for the next masterpiece. art national|banabae - we are all artists art brand-led the dream prize for any kid who loves clothes and creativity. banabae - the aussie kids’ clothing brand - turns the winner’s artwork into a real product in their next collection. winner takes home a $500 voucher plus their design printed onto actual banabae wares. four runners-up get $50 vouchers each. art national|camp australia big art comp art brand-led australia’s biggest oshc provider runs a national art comp every single term. hundreds of kids enter each round. past prizes have included custom hoodies featuring kids’ own artwork, lego creative happy boxes, $50 art shed vouchers, and a grand prize trophy designed by the brickman himself. real artist kerry evitts judges each round. art national|eckersley’s kids colouring competition art brand-led eckersley’s art & craft is australia’s beloved 60-year-old art supplies chain. kids pick up a free colouring sheet at any eckersley’s store (or download it online), colour it in any way they like - pencils, paints, crayons, anything goes - and submit. winners scoop $50 eckersley’s gift cards. art national|eckersley’s art & craft prize art brand-led launched 2025 to celebrate eckersley’s 60th anniversary. national exhibition at hazelhurst arts centre in september. while the headline prize targets adult artists, this one’s worth tracking for any youth/junior categories that may be added. art national|staedtler secondary school artist of the year art brand-led staedtler runs an annual high-school comp with a $5,000 prize pool. weekly random draw of $200 staedtler art packs throughout the entry period. plus a people’s choice voting round. three professional australian artists judge. art national|staedtler world kids colouring day art brand-led a global initiative by staedtler that’s been running for 18 years. kids submit a drawing on the year’s theme, and for every picture submitted staedtler donates to a plan international project supporting girls’ education - in 2026 this funds education for girls in malawi. art national (international)|smiggle christmas card competition art brand-led the cult aussie kids’ stationery brand runs an annual christmas card design comp. kids download a template, draw the front cover, colour it in - the winning design gets featured on actual smiggle christmas cards. prizes typically include vouchers and smiggle gear. art national|cartoon chef drawing competition art brand-led run by cartoon chef - the kids’ cartoon-drawing project that started as a regular feature in auspac newspapers in 2011. monthly drawing prompts, monthly winners. they also run an annual exhibition at the national cartoon gallery in coffs harbour. nsw creative kids voucher provider. art national|boathouse group kids colouring competition art brand-led the boathouse group runs sydney’s beloved waterfront eateries (manly, palm beach, shelly beach, balmoral). their kids’ colouring comp lands during school holidays with a kids hamper as the prize. art nsw (sydney)|lime tree kids colouring competition art brand-led lime tree kids is the aussie online toy and craft store run by an aussie mum. they run a seasonal colouring comp with a $100 voucher prize. art national|crayola creative acts of color (open call) art brand-led crayola’s ’creative acts of color’ is an open call rather than a traditional comp - kids share their creative work on social tagged @crayola and #staycreative. less about winning, more about being part of a global creative movement. crayola also runs an annual crayola creativity week (typically january). art international|micador brand giveaways art brand-led aussie owned art supplies brand. micador runs regular brand giveaways - ’win a year of micador,’ ’win a year of early start,’ etc. sub-brands include early start (toddlers), micador jr. (kids), micador (tweens) and micador for artists. art national|bunnings spring/seasonal art competitions art brand-led bunnings doesn’t run a national art comp consistently, but local stores run school-tied art comps - make your classroom sing like spring gave participating schools mdf boards and chubby pencil paints, and prizes included garden beds, gardening mix, and $50 bunnings vouchers. worth flagging that families/teachers can ask their local store about upcoming comps. art national (varies by store)|sydney royal easter show - junior arts & crafts art royal show australia’s biggest creativity showcase has been running since 1869 - approximately 5,500 exhibits across 500 categories. the junior art, craft & design competition has hundreds of classes for kids aged 2-20. winning entries displayed in the arts & crafts pavilion, the third-most-visited pavilion at the easter show. art national (nsw)|royal adelaide show - junior art, craft & design art royal show australia’s largest annual junior art, craft and design display. real prize money, real exhibition slots in the goyder pavilion. categories cover painting, drawing, digital photography, pottery, sewing, and dozens more. art sa|royal queensland show (ekka) - junior categories art royal show queensland’s biggest annual event runs one of the country’s largest creative competition rosters. junior art, photography, and craft categories sit alongside woodchop, giant vegetables and livestock. quintessentially aussie. art qld|nsw children’s week art competition art civic run by the nsw advocate for children and young people. the 2025 theme was ’everyone should know about children’s rights’ based on article 42 of the un convention on the rights of the child. group entries allowed and encouraged. three age categories with 1st, 2nd and 3rd place per category. art,culture nsw|children’s rights queensland art competition art civic run by children’s rights queensland in partnership with the queensland family and child commission. 2025 theme was ’every queensland child is loved, respected and has their rights upheld.’ over 300 entries received in 2025, with first/second/third place winners sharing $2,000+ in prizes across age groups. art,culture qld|world children’s picture contest (pentel) art international run by pentel of japan since 1970. one of the world’s oldest and largest international kids’ art comps - tens of thousands of entries from over 70 countries each year. themes vary annually. international recognition for any aussie kid who places. art international|international festival of owls kids’ art contest art international started in 2004 as a small us festival comp, now over 2,000 entries from dozens of countries. niche but enthusiastic - a perfect home for kids who love owls (and kids who love owls really love owls). no ai, no adult help. original art, posted to minnesota. art international (postal to usa)|embracing our differences art international florida-based but accepts entries globally. theme is consistent: ’enriching lives through diversity & inclusion.’ selected works displayed in an outdoor exhibition seen by 350,000+ visitors annually. art,culture international (us-based)|save the frogs! art contest art international frog conservation through art. junior (under 18) and student categories. aussie kids welcome. quirky, niche, surprisingly popular. art,environment international|whitlam institute what matters? writing competition writing a really special one. the whitlam institute asks kids one question - what matters? - and lets them answer however they want. last year over 6,500 students entered. year 5/6 winners get $350, a creative writing workshop, and an allen & unwin book pack. the overall winner takes home $1,500. every entry is read by a real human. writing,poetry national|nsw writeon competition writing the annual creative writing comp run by the nsw department of education in partnership with the state library. the 2026 stimulus: ’it was a small thing, but it made a difference.’ winning entries are published in the ’best of writeon’ anthology - a real book, kids’ words in print. writing nsw|dorothea mackellar poetry awards writing one of australia’s longest-running and most prestigious kids’ poetry comps, named after the woman who wrote ’my country.’ 2026’s optional theme is the traveller. cash prizes plus an annual anthology that publishes winners, runners-up, shortlisted and commended poems. entries can be solo, group, or whole-class. no ai. writing,poetry national|better read kids writing competition writing run by sydney’s beloved better read than dead bookstore. the 2026 theme is ’metamorphosis.’ every entry gets published in an anthology - so just by entering, kids become published writers. category winners score a $100 better read voucher, runners-up get $50. writing,poetry national|whitsunday voices short story competition writing cash prizes for first, second and third place in each age category. word limits step up with year level - 300-400 for grades 3-4, up to 1,200 for years 11-12. pure creative freedom on subject matter. strictly no ai. writing national|laura literary awards (prose & poetry) writing run by the rocky river writers club out of country sa. a lovely small-but-mighty comp with two streams - prose and poetry (cj dennis poetry awards). $25 to junior winners, $15 to junior primary. note: entries must be posted, not emailed. writing,poetry national|furphy story junior and youth competition writing a regional victoria gem. 1st prize $300, 2nd $100, 3rd $50 - in both story and poetry. generous prize money for a regional comp. writing,poetry vic - regional only|cbca wa’s make your own storybook awards writing make a real book - cover to cover, original text, original illustrations, hand-bound. solo or duo. run by the children’s book council of australia (wa). the most ’you’ve actually made a book’ feel of any kids’ comp out there. strictly no ai. writing,art wa|randolph stow young writers award writing cash prizes for primary writers in regional wa. winners get a perpetual trophy displayed in their school until end of term 2 the following year. two students from years 6-11 also win passes to the literature centre’s young writers collective program. writing,poetry wa - regional only|south perth young writers award (spywa) writing shortlisted entrants score a one-on-one workshop with a published local author for tailored feedback. finalists get prizes up to $150 and have their work published in a spywa anthology - one copy gifted to each finalist, one to their school library, one held in city of south perth libraries. writing wa - regional only|the golden pen (scribblers festival) writing run by scribblers festival, perth’s kids’ lit festival. the 2026 theme is metamorphosis. overall winner gets an e-reader and book pack ($249 value). shortlisted entrants get 6-month book subscriptions. bonus: classroom entries of 5+ can win a workshop with a scribblers creative. writing,poetry wa|cya conference hatchlings award writing run by the cya conference (children’s & young adults’ writers conference). solid cash prizes - $100 first, $60 second, $40 third. categories vary by writing form, with word counts to match. writing national|book links short story writing competition writing a nice low-key one for upper primary writers. $100 prize plus the winning story published on the book links website. open theme. writing national|just write - for kids (sa public libraries) writing run by marion city council’s library network. first prize up to $200, second up to $100. word limits 300-750 (9-10s) or 500-1,000 (11-13s). open theme. writing sa|state premier’s reading challenges writing reading not a competition - a challenge. hundreds of thousands of kids do this each year. read enough books from your state’s curated booklist and earn a certificate signed by the premier. the vibe is participation, not winning - but it’s a big motivating force for reluctant readers. each state runs its own version with similar mechanics. reading nsw, qld, vic, wa, sa, tas|crikey! magazine photography competition (australia zoo) photography & film run by australia zoo and the irwin family. big-ticket prizes: 2 nights at the crocodile hunter lodge (over $1,800 value), australia zoo family passes, signed gift baskets. robert irwin started his photography career here as a junior finalist. photography,environment national|australian geographic nature photographer of the year - junior category photography & film the big one. run by the south australian museum with australian geographic. junior winners take home $500, runners-up $250, plus all finalists get exhibited at the sa museum and australian museum. up to 4 entries per kid across categories like animals in nature, landscape, threatened species, macro, astrophotography. this is the comp robert irwin won as a kid. photography,environment national (and nz)|little sydney lives photography competition photography & film run by city of sydney as part of the australian life program. kids capture sydney through their own lens - phone snaps welcome, no fancy gear needed. from harbour sparkle to suburban stillness. selected works exhibit outdoors in central sydney. photography nsw (sydney)|australian museum ocean photography (young ocean photographer) photography & film linked to the australian museum’s ocean photographer of the year program. thr